<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Zelensky and Kushner confirm that Europe will join next round of Russia-Ukraine talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:349e60d31cdfee98693faa6e9dd56f834ae9ece4cdfd96b7ba8f7c445ea85ee5</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T01:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-live-zelensky-and-kushner-confirm-that-europe-will-join-next-round-of-russia-ukraine-talks--8ff08681f99f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-live-zelensky-and-kushner-confirm-that-europe-will-join-next-round-of-russia-ukraine-talks" /><summary type="html">US envoy and President ​Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner said on Thursday Russia and ​Ukraine ‌agreed ⁠to expand the next ‌round of talks to include ⁠European nations, who will debate whether their envoy should be one individual or more and who should represent them at a summit in Dublin on Friday. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia using 'illegal and unethical means, knows Europe won't use same means back', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed761f5842a9b319eed407a662b47694af22d6cda546d99e5d905e602493cecb</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:19:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261112-russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says--11000ef3a7f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261112-russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says" /><summary type="html">There are mounting concerns across Europe that recent hoax threats and cyber attacks could be part of a massive hybrid warfare campaign. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Elisabeth Braw, Senior Fellow with the Atlantic Council’s Transatlantic Security Initiative. She says that Russia's aim is to "increase its power at the expense of European countries and the easiest way to do that is to constantly wage this dirty war against European countries, using illegal and unethical means, because Russia knows that we are not going to use the same means back".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Russia using 'illegal and unethical means, knows Europe won't use same means back', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a56b7fbc7d24892616efe691c733b754add493af4270aa03b8fbb9992b7b0ec7</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:12:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says--1a4b49323855.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says" /><summary type="html">There are mounting concern across Europe that recent hoax threats and cyber attacks could be part of a massive hybrid warfare campaign. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Elisabeth Braw, Senior Fellow with the Atlantic Council’s Transatlantic Security Initiative. She says that Russia's aim is to "increase its power at the expense of European countries and the easiest way to do that is to constantly wage this dirty war against European countries, using illegal and unethical means, because Russia knows that we are not going to use the same means back".</summary></entry><entry><title>Mauritania fishing boats falsely portrayed as migrant fleet bound for Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67ff515e40428d7cd636344a262736f145c3bd0107dacd880d5352fe2b4f9f88</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T21:56:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261112-mauritania-fishing-boats-falsely-portrayed-as-migrant-fleet-bound-for-spain--95715b98438a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261112-mauritania-fishing-boats-falsely-portrayed-as-migrant-fleet-bound-for-spain" /><summary type="html">Spain’s Canary Islands are facing renewed pressure from migrant arrivals, with local authorities declaring a state of emergency. Against this backdrop, a viral video claims to show thousands of boats in Mauritania amassing at the port, that users said was "ready to set sail" to carry migrants to the archipelago. But the satellite images are misleading: they show a traditional fishing port, not a fleet of migrant vessels. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky warns Europe over US-Russia talks on broader security arrangements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a5c7e6f07e964819f54ce97ea79263cfbed5842e83123c45d2de084734c40ea</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T19:53:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-europe-over-us-russia-talks-on-broader-security-arrangements--514193c26030.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-europe-over-us-russia-talks-on-broader-security-arrangements" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned European leaders Thursday to be wary of discussions between the United States and Russia about a new security arrangement for the continent. Before launching the war in 2022, the Kremlin delivered an ultimatum to NATO on Europe's security arrangements which included demands for the alliance to withdraw forces from eastern Europe and stop accepting new members. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's Vladimir Putin suggests no Ukraine compromise in meeting with US envoys</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d82d4c874d263b3e07136d43cc9f7f7dc4ca7724daa3e1daa0aa6db5cf27fde</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys--26ef97037a98.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys" /><summary type="html">Russia's President Vladimir Putin indicated on Thursday, November 12, that the Kremlin would not compromise on its hardline demands to end the war in Ukraine, but offered a short-term ceasefire in a key frontline city during a meeting with US envoys. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Five men on trial for murder of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci's brother</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4d094a78bb4133f8a12685928e33a8ff4f2c88f91d8715678501a0330912e44</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:20:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother--97c5322846e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother" /><summary type="html">In France, the trial of five men accused of murdering the brother of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci is under way. Amine Kessaci, originally known as an environmental activist, became a prominent figure in the fight against drug-related crime after losing two of his brothers to violence linked to drug trafficking. The defendants face the possibility of life imprisonment. The verdict is expected on Monday, November 16. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders gather in Dublin to discuss Ukraine's security, and their own</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b32bcd15c2077427f2717f221ac5f2f66c64597ce049016c9f9f9585e5a8b7b</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:19:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own--56692e996cbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own" /><summary type="html">Leaders from more than 40 European countries gathered in Dublin on Thursday, November 12, for a summit focused on the continent’s fragile security, amid a new US-backed effort to revive talks on ending the Russia-Ukraine war. The meeting of the European Political Community brought together heads of state and government from European countries and the UK, as well as Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney and NATO Secretary-General Mark Rutte.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of schools evacuated in Italy as bomb threats spread across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebee3cc6ef75a3cb782cd682e2157efb62fe7e9c12689cd31175baaf6c26d860</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:08:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe--85c832b8d0d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". The threats come after a series of hoax bomb alerts across Europe in recent weeks, which have prompted growing concern about the possibility of an escalation in hybrid warfare.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31: Climate disruption puts farmers and global food supplies under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c448a44a1ba2b590a4685c7421640388e2d89874d492b593f6c7f590ec073b59</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:04:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure--703bcb8d3e50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure" /><summary type="html">As delegates gather in Turkey for the COP31 climate conference, discussions are focusing on emissions and climate targets. But humanitarian agencies are highlighting another urgent consequence of climate disruption: growing food insecurity. With the return of El Niño adding to concerns over extreme weather and its impact on food production, the Food and Agriculture Organisation is calling for food systems to be placed at the heart of climate action.</summary></entry><entry><title>New restrictions to Starshield network 'kill more Ukrainians', Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6718f613c20ec22b354116b2fd28d7ca24b4e34a31ec5c3220b57d5a31a467f4</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:06:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says--b63c57dc57ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ⁠President Volodymyr Zelensky ​on Thursday said that Ukrainian ​military units had recorded new and significant disruptions to the Starshield satellite communications service in recent days, affecting ​the ‌entire front ⁠line and Russian-occupied parts of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's 'hidden mobilization': The 'expendable' lives fueling Putin's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94564427e4b20c34de21898fc4f3a195ad5182ff9c502b1291d87a6f15596277</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:39:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-hidden-mobilization-the-expendable-lives-fueling-putin-s-war-on-ukraine--f5e8509ede95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-hidden-mobilization-the-expendable-lives-fueling-putin-s-war-on-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome John Lough, Senior Research Fellow and Head of Foreign Policy &amp; International Partnerships at the New Eurasian Strategies Centre (NEST Centre), He is also an Associate Fellow with the Russia &amp; Eurasia Programme at Chatham House. Lough offers a sobering assessment of the social and strategic dynamics sustaining Russia's invasion of Ukraine. He argues that the Kremlin has disproportionately recruited soldiers from poorer and politically marginalised communities, including ethnic minority regions, where the human cost of the conflict is less likely to generate organised opposition. Many of those recruited, he explains, "have been recruited for a deliberate reason because they were seen, you know, ultimately as lives that were expendable, in other words as cannon fodder."</summary></entry><entry><title>US envoys arrive in Dublin for meeting with Zelensky and European representatives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95bc34f5177a00dc7e6f58740b0a142a3a94668bdc5db3dbde628e227c5a42e</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T02:31:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks--eb0f36381594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks" /><summary type="html">US special envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Dublin Thursday night to meet Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky following their talks with his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin in Moscow. Representatives from France, Germany, Britain and potentially other European nations will also join the discussions, a diplomatic source said. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>European leaders gather in Dublin under the shadow of hybrid threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2d042f82b3c2c8e3ec85fa5e81a4115e91a359dbcb471973f9b887bc3beec54</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T22:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-under-the-shadow-of-hybrid-threats--ebbc2bf82ef8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-under-the-shadow-of-hybrid-threats" /><summary type="html">Ireland is mounting the largest security operation in its history as around 50 European leaders gather in Dublin this week amid growing concerns over hybrid attacks. The operation follows a wave of hoax bomb threats targeting airlines and media organisations across Europe, with Irish police reporting new incidents on Monday and Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Olivia Bizot reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine agree to major prisoner swap as peace talks end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73ea7d20644d17652adbed937c2bf79cd0a68204c4ed2d9072a5b056d2def80e</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:46:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end--e9c04d147348.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end" /><summary type="html">Kyiv and Moscow on Wednesday agreed to a large-scale prisoner exchange as the final day of peace talks in Abu Dhabi came to an end, though neither side gave a concrete figure. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will meet separately with Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky on Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out hundreds of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c1b83f6570adbf54b3f7e6b861427a3857b611787b96ee5a55d5f6d512c88c2</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain--305c14ca2c0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Millions of workers in Spain shut down businesses and public transport on Wednesday, as part of the country's first general strike in 14 years. Following a peaceful march in Barcelona over soaring rents and property prices, and the rising cost of living, protesters smashed storefronts, set off small bonfires, burned bins and launched fireworks towards police. The unrest comes just weeks before snap elections, called by Socialist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out tens of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ac505c8d44b6d72debb0d222f1e6c7e0245020c80a84edaf9d029b8b3034120</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:37:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain--b3f1fe2dfc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched across Spain on Wednesday during a general strike over housing affordability and purchasing power just weeks before an early general election. Unions reported a significant response in some sectors in Spain's first nationwide 24-hour stoppage since 2012, but business leaders played down the participation. Braving heavy rain, tens of thousands of demonstrators marched through central Madrid carrying placards shaped like houses and chanting "We have no home" as they called for more affordable housing. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days after shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26cf7eb5579450e4b987814faafc4f23c2b64a8166d938dc989d027ab4cd9382</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:31:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1--6aff4f4e4234.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. The event is a magnet for all shades of Poland's right wing -- from conservative-nationalists aligned with its Law and Justice (PiS) party to far-right and radical groups. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Schools evacuated across Italy after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d8482cad6708a45fb02d0ad0200e516316f431471272f2ca994fcc8a5a12264</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:29:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats--8b8597a1d133.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". Similar hoax threats were reported in schools in Britain and Ireland, which reportedly prompted some evacuations in Scotland. Meloni said she had called a government meeting with security and intelligence chiefs for Wednesday to discuss the threats. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days afer shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b02bb5617a9cacae30e52e36b350396e5ed74669bc084092ccbb20ebf7323c57</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:08:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings--f224bca0510d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. While generally peaceful, some rallies in the pasthave been marred by clashes with police or counter-demonstrators. Philip Turle gives us his take.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia bans two French lawmakers and two journalists from entry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3645f23b949e5bc35b9ff59d723b04707705de8416eb15738a1da3b827e00a3a</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry--647f8165ba44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Wednesday said it was banning two French journalists and two French lawmakers from entering Russia in response to Paris's expulsion of pro-Russian TV commentator Xenia Fedorova earlier this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb3193d49677c1258d7fd8ac5ef775068b856733bbcf7d868037cb8948a6b59</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:54:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election--d795ce513ad5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cd1af68f3cdb0f5d05a0445cb946836d6eda17c84a91c22b66109f848ec4089</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions--7f31e05dcc4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Aneto, one of southern Europe's largest glaciers, is melting away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa30a57158ee59afa925cf839d2bc4afa8ba8022456bae626ac82fba7bd3adf0</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away--7bca17aca8fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away" /><summary type="html">Within a decade, one of the largest glaciers in southern Europe will have disappeared. Aneto, the highest peak of the Spanish Pyrenees, is melting at a spectacular rate. Its demise is another sign of global warming and has much to teach glaciologists. FRANCE 24's Maude Petit-Jové, Mathilde Lopinski and Sarah Morris report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Patrick Bury: 'It’s going to cost a lot of money to repair the systems.'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcee0fe3f07068638c0254e493d574514ad674bf6256673a7fcfbb3d11415c6e</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict--d7020f165247.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict" /><summary type="html">Patrick Bury, Senior associate professor in warfare and counterterrorism at University of Bath, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK comedian David Walliams accused of grooming and sexual harassment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2960c932574a6ab6fa0c25fa8ad3d07e122f495347b4ce0c31083eebec55b3d9</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment--5fccf1ffbe7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, November 11: Spanish and French papers discuss protests in the two countries. An investigation by The Guardian and ITV accuses comedian David Walliams of "preying on young women for sex". Finally, a Doberman sensed something was wrong with a baby. It may have saved his life.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Wave of hoax bomb threats sent to schools in UK, Ireland and Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c421b94824203a5ee75a701e69d75c0808a06262210c1f4f677ff3f08a6020df</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats--967169548911.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of schools in the UK, Italy and the Republic of Ireland received a "generic" threatening email on Wednesday now being treated as a hoax by authorities. Italy earlier evacuated roughly 300 schools over the perceived threat.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine start second day of US-led talks: Kyiv lead negotiator</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1246e7ad910c733a83f704901d5748ec4611e89bec9e9b46d4c1facc3fdb744c</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:42:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator--ce553d61579f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine have resumed US-mediated talks in Abu Dhabi for a second day, Kyiv's chief negotiator Rustem Umerov said on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's first general strike in 14 years, 3 weeks before national polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5617c5cb45c0f03ee54227cda0f351a34a6a6b721f09e8fda497b30af1e547a3</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:30:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-first-general-strike-in-14-years-3-weeks-before-national-polls--7baf50b0712f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-first-general-strike-in-14-years-3-weeks-before-national-polls" /><summary type="html">Sarah Morris is live from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Portugal shuts schools, tech conference as it braces for storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c960b0a11201c96445c9bceaf87b85d7d5011b7a0261c26d301f33361dd8f77e</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/portugal-shuts-schools-tech-conference-as-it-braces-for-storm--85bdf5a4749a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/portugal-shuts-schools-tech-conference-as-it-braces-for-storm" /><summary type="html">Portugal said it would shut schools, non-essential services and a top world tech conference on Wednesday, as it braces for gale-force winds of Storm Charles.</summary></entry></feed>
